Draft a memorial of gratitude for the bestowal of a banquet after His Majesty visited the Western Park (Xiyuan), took his seat in the Hall of Against Luxurious Ease (Wuyi dian), and commanded the Grand Secretaries to sit and lecture on the "Against Luxurious Ease" (Wuyi) chapter of the Book of Documents (Shangshu) and the "Seventh Month" (Qiyue) ode from the "Airs of Bin" (Binfeng) in the Book of Odes (Shi) [tenth year of the Jiajing reign (1531)].

Legal Judgments [five items]:
Issuing service-record certificates for officials and subofficial functionaries;
Lands of meritorious officials;
Presenting memorials to set forth views;
Reporting on military affairs;
Clarifying grievances and false accusations.

Third Session
Policy Questions [five items]:
Question: In establishing governance and examining plans, nothing is greater than deliberation. Yao had his inquiries in the Chamber of the Crossroads (Qushi), and Shun had his consultations in the Hall of Assemblage (Zongzhang); both refer to deliberation. Our Dynasty has enjoyed successive eras of splendor and harmony for over two hundred years now, and all institutions and regulations have been brilliantly established in full—such as deliberating on the calendar epoch, deliberating on the fixing of the suburban sacrifices, deliberating on the breached Yellow River at Zhangqiu, and deliberating on the pacification…
